{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Antwerp, 8 October 1822\n\nMy dearest Marie,\n\nThe journey has been wearying, but the mind has found its rest. We walked the field of Waterloo for four hours, the ground itself a witness to the turning of ages. It is a place where the spirit of the world felt its weight. In Brussels, the gallery and the church at Laeken offered a different kind of stillness, though the rectorate handover in Ghent was a necessary formality.\n\nWe left Ghent late, and the cabriolet carried us through the night. It is now past ten, and we are on the bank of the Scheldt, opposite the city. The air is cool, and the river dark. I am tired, but the road has been clear. I hope the boys are well and that your health is steady. I shall write again once we have settled.\n\nYour devoted,\nG. W. F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795220581,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":200,"prompt_tokens":1013,"total_tokens":1213,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-ZCaxqJMT0aavzGyNfNP05vuNehG6QFxV","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1013,"prompt_ms":1043.694,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.030300098716683,"prompt_per_second":970.5909969780415,"predicted_n":200,"predicted_ms":4776.916,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.00460301507538,"predicted_per_second":41.65867685343431}}